            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the issue!\r\n\r\n'mini.pick' is not responsible for this. It is an issue with terminal emulator and/or Neovim drawing Neovim's state. I can partially reproduce this in `st` terminal emulator, but not in `ghostty` or `kitty`. Those three have different (at least visually) ways of handling resizing terminal window, that's probably the reason. Even after reproducing it in `st`, one extra resize would make things as expected again.\r\n\r\nClosing as not an issue with 'mini.pick'.",
